{"title":"Career Roadmap · Gallery Assistant","role":"Gallery Assistant","summary":"A Gallery Assistant supports the day-to-day operation of an art gallery, museum, cultural institution, artist studio, auction environment, or exhibition space. The role can involve visitor assistance, artwork handling, exhibition preparation, documentation, inventory, research support, installation, event coordination, sales support, and communication with artists, curators, collectors, and visitors.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1 UG · 2026","Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Fine Arts (BA)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Build fine-art knowledge + art history + gallery operations + documentation + exhibition experience"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Choose gallery operations, exhibitions, collections, education, sales, or curatorial work"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Progress toward Gallery Coordinator, Exhibition Manager, Curatorial Associate or Arts Manager"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Combine art expertise with digital collections, cultural management, technology, audience development and global art networks"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Career-route check","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"BA Fine Arts is strongly aligned with Gallery Assistant work. However, a successful gallery professional needs more than artistic ability. Students should develop knowledge of art history, visual culture, exhibition practices, artwork documentation, collections handling, communication, event management, digital cataloguing and basic arts administration."},{"type":"p","text":"A practical route is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Fine Arts","Gallery/Museum Internship","Gallery Assistant","Gallery Coordinator / Exhibition Assistant","Gallery Manager / Curatorial Assistant","Curator / Arts Manager / Exhibition Manager"]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"These are practical career-planning horizons, not guaranteed promotion timelines."}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Drawing, visual language and art appreciation"},{"text":"BA Fine Arts curriculum + museum/gallery resources"},{"text":"Artwork portfolio + exhibition visits"},{"text":"Artistic foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Art history fundamentals"},{"text":"Museum collections + academic resources"},{"text":"Annotated artwork research file"},{"text":"Art knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Gallery operations"},{"text":"Exhibition visits + gallery projects"},{"text":"Gallery operations checklist"},{"text":"Industry awareness"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Artwork documentation"},{"text":"Museum/gallery catalogues"},{"text":"25–50 professionally documented artworks"},{"text":"Documentation"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Exhibition planning"},{"text":"College exhibitions + curatorial projects"},{"text":"Mini exhibition proposal"},{"text":"Exhibition skills"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Internship + visitor engagement"},{"text":"Gallery/museum internship"},{"text":"Internship report + references"},{"text":"Professional exposure"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Curatorial/research skills"},{"text":"Art research + exhibition projects"},{"text":"Curatorial essay/catalogue"},{"text":"Research"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Job-ready portfolio"},{"text":"Gallery internship + exhibition work"},{"text":"CV + portfolio + exhibition credits"},{"text":"Employability"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core Knowledge Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Fine Arts Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Drawing"},{"text":"Painting"},{"text":"Sculpture"},{"text":"Printmaking"},{"text":"Photography"},{"text":"Installation art"},{"text":"Digital art"},{"text":"Mixed media"},{"text":"Contemporary art"},{"text":"Visual composition"},{"text":"Colour theory"},{"text":"Art criticism"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student does not necessarily need to become a professional practising artist, but should be able to understand, discuss and professionally document artworks."},{"type":"h","text":"2. Art History"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Indian art history"},{"text":"Western art history"},{"text":"Modern art"},{"text":"Contemporary art"},{"text":"Modern Indian art"},{"text":"Regional art traditions"},{"text":"Indigenous and folk art"},{"text":"Sculpture traditions"},{"text":"Photography history"},{"text":"Digital and new-media art"},{"text":"Major artistic movements"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to identify:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Artist","Artwork","Medium","Period","Movement","Context","Subject","Technique","Interpretation"]}]},{"heading":"Gallery Operations","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand how a gallery functions."},{"type":"h","text":"Before an exhibition"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Artist coordination"},{"text":"Artwork selection"},{"text":"Artwork inventory"},{"text":"Condition documentation"},{"text":"Artwork labels"},{"text":"Cataloguing"},{"text":"Installation planning"},{"text":"Transportation coordination"},{"text":"Insurance documentation"},{"text":"Marketing support"}]},{"type":"h","text":"During an exhibition"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Visitor assistance"},{"text":"Artwork monitoring"},{"text":"Gallery etiquette"},{"text":"Artist/collector assistance"},{"text":"Event coordination"},{"text":"Visitor feedback"},{"text":"Sales support where applicable"},{"text":"Security coordination"}]},{"type":"h","text":"After an exhibition"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Deinstallation"},{"text":"Artwork return"},{"text":"Inventory reconciliation"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Photography"},{"text":"Sales records"},{"text":"Exhibition report"},{"text":"Archive update"}]}]},{"heading":"Artwork Documentation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is one of the most valuable practical skills for an entry-level gallery professional."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to record:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Artist"},{"text":"Artwork title"},{"text":"Year"},{"text":"Medium"},{"text":"Dimensions"},{"text":"Edition number"},{"text":"Signature"},{"text":"Provenance information"},{"text":"Acquisition information"},{"text":"Current location"},{"text":"Condition"},{"text":"Exhibition history"},{"text":"Image"},{"text":"Copyright/usage information"},{"text":"Inventory ID"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Example"},{"type":"note","label":"Artist","text":"Artist Name\nTitle: Untitled\nYear: 2027\nMedium: Acrylic on canvas\nDimensions: 90 × 120 cm\nInventory ID: GA-2027-014\nCondition: Good\nExhibition: Student Contemporary Art Exhibition 2027"}]},{"heading":"Collections & Artwork Handling","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Gallery Assistant should understand basic professional handling."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Safe artwork movement"},{"text":"Proper packing"},{"text":"Framing basics"},{"text":"Handling works on paper"},{"text":"Handling paintings"},{"text":"Sculpture handling"},{"text":"Photography documentation"},{"text":"Environmental considerations"},{"text":"Storage organisation"},{"text":"Condition reporting"},{"text":"Installation safety"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For valuable or fragile collections, students should follow the institution's professional conservation and handling procedures rather than improvising."}]},{"heading":"Exhibition Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Exhibition concept"},{"text":"Artist selection"},{"text":"Artwork selection"},{"text":"Floor plans"},{"text":"Gallery layout"},{"text":"Display height"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Artwork labels"},{"text":"Wall text"},{"text":"Catalogue preparation"},{"text":"Opening events"},{"text":"Visitor flow"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Exhibition documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mini exhibition exercise"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a hypothetical exhibition:"},{"type":"note","label":"Theme","text":"Contemporary Indian Identity"},{"type":"p","text":"Then prepare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Exhibition statement"},{"text":"10-artwork shortlist"},{"text":"Artist biographies"},{"text":"Gallery floor plan"},{"text":"Artwork labels"},{"text":"Wall text"},{"text":"Exhibition catalogue"},{"text":"Social-media campaign"},{"text":"Opening-event plan"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This becomes a strong portfolio project."}]},{"heading":"Digital Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microsoft Excel"},{"text":"Google Sheets"},{"text":"PowerPoint"},{"text":"Canva"},{"text":"Adobe Photoshop"},{"text":"Adobe InDesign"},{"text":"Adobe Lightroom"},{"text":"Basic photo editing"},{"text":"Digital asset management"},{"text":"File naming and organisation"},{"text":"Online exhibition platforms"},{"text":"Social media"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful creative software can include Adobe Creative Cloud.","url":"https://www.adobe.com/creativecloud.html"}]},{"heading":"Arts Administration","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Exhibition budgets"},{"text":"Vendor coordination"},{"text":"Event planning"},{"text":"Artist contracts"},{"text":"Purchase orders"},{"text":"Invoices"},{"text":"Sponsorship"},{"text":"Grants"},{"text":"Gallery sales"},{"text":"Client communication"},{"text":"Collector relations"},{"text":"Marketing"},{"text":"Public relations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A Gallery Assistant who understands both art and administration can progress faster into gallery-management roles."},{"type":"h","text":"Projects to Build Before Graduation"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Artwork Catalogue"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a catalogue of 30–50 artworks with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Artist"},{"text":"Title"},{"text":"Medium"},{"text":"Dimensions"},{"text":"Year"},{"text":"Image"},{"text":"Description"},{"text":"Category"},{"text":"Inventory number"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Gallery Exhibition Plan"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a complete exhibition including:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Theme"},{"text":"Artist selection"},{"text":"Artwork selection"},{"text":"Floor plan"},{"text":"Wall labels"},{"text":"Exhibition statement"},{"text":"Visitor journey"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Artist Research Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Research five artists and prepare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Biography"},{"text":"Major works"},{"text":"Artistic style"},{"text":"Medium"},{"text":"Influences"},{"text":"Major exhibitions"},{"text":"Critical reception"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Condition Report"},{"type":"p","text":"Create sample condition reports for paintings, sculptures and works on paper."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Gallery Social Media"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a one-month content plan:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Artist spotlight"},{"text":"Artwork of the week"},{"text":"Exhibition announcement"},{"text":"Behind the scenes"},{"text":"Curatorial story"},{"text":"Visitor content"},{"text":"Exhibition closing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 6 — Virtual Exhibition"},{"type":"p","text":"Create an online exhibition with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Exhibition theme"},{"text":"Digital artworks"},{"text":"Artist descriptions"},{"text":"Curatorial statement"},{"text":"Virtual gallery layout"},{"text":"Digital catalogue"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation Options"},{"type":"table","header":["Lane","Core stack","Senior role it leads to"],"rows":[[{"text":